Subject: [PATCH] em_cli: name a native agent on a wired backhaul an extender

em_cli named every agent attached over Ethernet "Agent-N" in traversal
order, which assumed the gateway's co-located agent was the only one. A
native extender on a wired backhaul (its LAN port bridged into the
controller's LAN) took "Agent-1" and pushed the gateway's agent to
"Agent-2", while the lab relies on Agent-1 being the gateway.

The network's CollocatedAgentID names the co-located agent: it alone is an
Agent; any other wired native agent is an Extender like its Wi-Fi peers.
Without a known co-located agent the naming is as before.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/rdkb-cli/device_naming_test.go
